  "decision_conditions": [
    "No legal agreement is in place to prohibit future residents from applying for parking permits or parking in the retained parking spaces (noted as allocated for commercial business users within the area). In the absence of a such an agreement, residents could park in the spaces allocated for commercial use. This would lead to displacement of parking on to surroundings roads and areas, which would not be in the best interests of Highway safety. Furthermore, the development would not be car free and would therefore put undue pressure on nearby Controlled Parking Zones, leading to additional parking displacement and adverse highways impacts. Consequently, the proposal would be contrary to Policy DMT 2 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (January 2020), Policy T4 of the London Plan (2021) and paragraph 116 of the NPPF (2024).",
    "The decision to REFUSE planning permission has been taken having regard to all relevant planning legislation, regulations, guidance, circulars and Council policies, including The Human Rights Act (1998) (HRA 1998) which makes it unlawful for the Council to act incompatibly with Convention rights, specifically Article 6 (right to a fair hearing); Article 8 (right to respect for private and family life); Article 1 of the First Protocol (protection of property) and Article 14 (prohibition of discrimination).",
    "The decision to REFUSE planning permission has been taken having regard to the policies and proposals in the Hillingdon Local Plan Part 1 (2012) and Part 2 (2020) set out below, including Supplementary Planning Guidance, and to all relevant material considerations, including The London Plan (2021) and NPPF (2024)."
  ],
